  "netlist_origin": "Copied unmodified from simulation/harness/nets/zvs_margin_sweep.cir, then only .include paths were rewritten to absolute paths (the file moved out of simulation/harness/nets/) and .param overrides applied the same way run_zvs_sweep.py's override_params() does.",
  "why_this_exists": "Both official harnesses (run_zvs_sweep.py, run_tank_coil_sweep.py) were re-run before and after the pan_load.sub correction and produced BYTE-IDENTICAL results (see docs/evidence/2026-07-27-pan-model-correction.md table). This is because zvs_margin_sweep.cir's X_PAN instantiation line explicitly overrides ALL FIVE PANLOAD_TRANSFORMER parameters (L1, L2, K, RPAN, RCOIL) via .cir-level .param statements, and neither harness script exposes PAN_L2 as an overridable sweep axis -- their PAN_K/PAN_RPAN preset values are literal Python constants (run_zvs_sweep.py:121-127), not read from pan_load.sub. Correcting pan_load.sub's subckt DEFAULTS therefore cannot change either official harness's output. This supplementary sweep exists to answer the question those two harnesses structurally cannot: what does the corrected model actually imply, end-to-end, in the real half-bridge + tank topology.",
