    "summary": "With PANLOAD_TRANSFORMER's corrected parameters (K=0.79, L2=218uH, RPAN=10ohm), the pan-loaded tank's resonant frequency is far higher than the broken model implied (e.g. 55.9kHz vs the old model's 34.7kHz at L1=70uH -- a 61% shift), because the corrected coupling reduces apparent inductance to ~39-40% of L1 instead of ~99.99%. At the ZVS-held optimum for every L tested (70/90/110/130/150uH), delivered power is 5266-10239W -- FAR EXCEEDING 1800W, the opposite conclusion from the pre-correction model's 'unreachable at every L tested.' This is a SUPPLEMENTARY, non-harness result (see why_this_exists) and does not modify or supersede the two official evidence artifacts, which are unaffected by this correction."
